{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/515788-help-with-a-write-up-for-orihime-zhin\u00fc-the-star-festival-s-weaving-princess","id":515788,"title":"Help with a write-up for Orihime/Zhin\u00fc, the Star Festival's Weaving-Princess?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-15T21:19:34-07:00","id":515788,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Help with a write-up for Orihime/Zhin\u00fc, the Star Festival's Weaving-Princess?","content":"<img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/ov0X6ss.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Hi everybody! I was going to propose playing a scion of the Weaving Princess (and ostensibly the Cow-herder's reincarnation). Tell the truth, I was a little shocked that she wasn't included in the Celestial Bureaucracy, considering the popularity of her holiday across East Asia and Indochina. <br /> <br /> If you haven't heard of Tanabata/ the Qixi Festival here are the wiki links:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanabata\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/df/Fussa_Tanabata_Festival-Tokyo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanabata\" target=\"_blank\"> Tanabata - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanabata\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanabata </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qixi_Festival\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Qijiepan_for_the_Seven_Sisters_-_Hong_Kong_Museum_of_History_-_DSC00942.JPG/1280px-Qijiepan_for_the_Seven_Sisters_-_Hong_Kong_Museum_of_History_-_DSC00942.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qixi_Festival\" target=\"_blank\"> Qixi Festival - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qixi_Festival\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qixi_Festival </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I will say that there is a lot of variation in the myths. One variant was that it rained on Earth because of the tears of the Shen crying over the loss of such a wonderful girl like Zhinu. Another variant was that through her weavings Orihime was able to tell the future, and this ocular ability was the reason the Sky King didn't want to let his daughter marry the Cow-herder. However, a common profile is consistent through most myths. Orihime/Zhinu was stunningly beautiful, and this beauty was more than skin deep. The Weaving Princess was adored by all of Heaven, and no one could find an ill word to be spoken about her. The Weaving Princess was an outstanding weaver and seamstress, and product of which the Sky King jealously guards close. The Weaving Princess is in True Love with the Cow-herder and would spend all her time with him, if it was not for her Father's interdiction. Rather than raging against the heavens, she is the embodiment of the perfect and dutiful daughter and obeys her Father. She is eternally optimistic, looking forward to the next time she can see her love.<br /> <br /> From this I think we have enough to build a stat block.<br /> <br /> Orihime/Zhin\u00fc<br /> Aliases: Thread-Weaving Princess, Morning Glory Princess, Spider Princess, the Favorite Daughter of Heaven.<br /> Favored Previews: Epic Appearance, Epic Dexterity, Animal (Spider), Stars, Prophecy (Tsukumo-Gami OR Taiyi)<br /> Favored Skills: Craft, Politics, Presence, Empathy, Occult<br /> <br /> How is this for a write-up. Would you be convinced to add Lady Orihime as a Goddess in your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T23:17:46-07:00","id":515864,"title":"","content":"I'm not familiar with the Deity myself, but the write up looks pretty good from my position. I only have a couple questions that may result in it being tweaked.<br /> <br /> 1) She has Epic Dexterity. This gives her great combat ability (Making her one of the greatest warriors) and Speed, when what I think your going for is intricate body control Ala Weaving and Artistic crafts. Would it be better to change it to the Forge Purview instead? Perhaps give her a unique knack/trait/birthright to build her arts with Intelligence or Appearance?<br /> <br /> 2) You give her the Stars Purview but I don't really see any justification in your writeup? Strangely enough Stars in Scion 1E do not refer to the actual stars, but are basically control of Time. Does she possess that power?<br /> <br /> Aside from that it looks quite reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T07:52:50-07:00","id":516188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wingnut2292</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/515788-help-with-a-write-up-for-orihime-zhin\u00fc-the-star-festival-s-weaving-princess#post515788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everybody! I was going to propose playing a scion of the Weaving Princess (and ostensibly the Cow-herder's reincarnation). Tell the truth, I was a little shocked that she wasn't included in the Celestial Bureaucracy, considering the popularity of her holiday across East Asia and Indochina.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a LOT that is omitted. If the writers tried to fit it all they'd have less of a game and more of an encyclopedia.<br /> <br /> BUT I LOVE WHERE YOUR HEAD IS AT!<br /> <br /> Damn good picture too.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T18:57:06-07:00","id":516639,"title":"","content":"<br /> Thanks for the feedback everyone! Based on the feedback everyone has given, here's a revised write up.<br /> <br /> Orihime/Zhin\u00fc<br /> Aliases: Thread-Weaving Princess, Morning Glory Princess, Spider Princess, the Favorite Daughter of Heaven.<br /> Favored Previews: Epic Appearance, Epic Charisma, Animal (Spider), Forge, Moon, Prophecy (Tsukumo-Gami OR Taiyi)<br /> Favored Skills: Craft, Politics, Presence, Empathy, Occult<br /> <br /> When in the World, Orihime/Zhin\u00fc assumes rolls that blend artistry and Asian mystery. She's been an artist who makes dresses out of spidersilk and the daughter of the Yellow Peril himself. Most frequently, her trips into the World are discreet preparations for her one day with the Cow-herder, making small changes to seemingly random things that have profound effect on That Day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T19:03:48-07:00","id":516643,"title":"","content":"*poke head in* Shen senses are tingling!<br /> <br /> Okay but in all seriousness, I just rewrote the Shen and Kami a few months ago, it's probably on the first page still.<br /> <br /> Vega's a fun character but I'm looking at your associated powers and staring confusedly. She's got no other myths to my knowledge besides Cowherd and Vega (if I'm wrong please let me know), and so I'm baffled as to where most of these came from. My main references for this are Chen Lianshan's <i>Chinese Myths and Legends</i> and Michael Ashkenazi's <i>Handbook of Japanese Mythology</i>, if you want my sources.<br /> <br /> I'll break it down piece by piece.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>- Ehhhhhh?? If you have to give her an Epic, it'd probably be this. As a supernatural figure, she is certainly described as beautiful.<br /> <b>Dexterity</b>- I'm confused as to why she's getting this as an associated power. Because she weaves? That would give her Art and/or Craft, most likely. (Given how poetry oriented Tanabata is, I'd give her both)<br /> <b>Animal </b>(Spider)- Wait what? I can't find anything linking Vega to Spiders, at all. Chinese myth usually links weavers to Silkworms, a la Leizu. The closest thing I can find to link her to an animal is Magpies, and that's kind of tenuous.<br /> <b>Stars</b>- I think literally being turned into a star is reason enough to be given Stars, no objection from me. Her festival, Tanabata merely strengthens this connection.<br /> <b>Prophecy</b>- Another &quot;Wait, what?&quot; In what myth does Vega divine the future?<br /> <b>Tsukumogami/Taiyi</b>- *Shameless plug for my own new PsP's for these two pantheons, Harae and Dao, respectively* But in any case, I'd most likely make her a minor Shen, but her myth is so pervasive I could see one arguing for her inclusion in either. She's like Guan Yin.<br /> *Immediately after I posted this, the thread updated with your changes*<br /> <b>Charisma</b>: Another Ehhhhhhhh. See Appearance.<br /> <b>Forge</b>: She doesn't do that? You get Forge for doing massively important things with creation. Inventing new art forms and producing legendary artifacts and such. Weaving is Vega's title but she doesn't invent anything. Again with the Crafts association.<br /> <b>Moon</b>: Again, confusion. Where and When did she become a lunar goddess?<br /> <br /> Note on abilities: Forgot one! Gods get 6. Like I said above, I'd give her Art. Occult's iffy, but I can't think of anything better to replace it. Academics maybe?<br /> <br /> It kind of looks like you based your write up on the Celestial Bureaucracy in Companion, which while understandable (lord knows I did some awful writeups based on it), the entirety of Companion was kind of awful and most of the god write ups make zero sense. Just look at how every Dev and Devi have a million associated powers. With a figure like Vega, she doesn't have a lot of wiggle room for associated powers due to being a figure in one myth and one myth only.<br /> <br /> *Also the phrase &quot;Asian Mystery&quot; is hilariously vague and pretty Orientalist. Like, she <i>is</i> Asian, it ain't a mystery to her or her people.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1012,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1012-sorcerymon","user":"Sorcerymon","date":". 05-16-2015, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1012-sorcerymon","name":"Sorcerymon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1012_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}